WEBVTT

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.830
Wh-Where am I?

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:20.580
I...

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.060
What happened?

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.680
It's not working.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.050
Where is this place?

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.950
I must've crash-landed.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:56.660
<i>It's an island.</i>

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.290
Isn't that...

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.080
Hina.

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:17.000
I-It won't open.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:18.970
Hina.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.180
Hina. Wake up, Hina.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.090
Hina!

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:31.130
Spread your wings

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:35.750
See the light of hope in the sky you have yet to witness

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:39.050
And don't ever give in to the weight of sorrow

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:44.430
Echo unto eternity, "Unisonia"

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:53.690
That world you see before your eyes

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:59.280
I wonder what colors it is made of

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.740
The pain of loss isn't something

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.700
You want to get used to, and yet

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:11.670
Even on a night like this, the stars glisten

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:18.630
Like a tarnished coin spilling from the palm of your hand

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.470
Can't go back

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:21.880
Want to go home

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:25.220
The two of them back-to-back

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.260
Break through

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:32.020
Turning unfading emotions into a lasting bond

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:35.360
Like painting over a colorless world

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:38.070
Let this sympathy reach

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:44.320
Let's build the future that we envision

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:47.530
You'll see, we'll even change fate

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:52.330
Transcending time, "Unisonia"

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:04.330
Why?

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:07.750
Why won't you let us search for Ensign Ryazan?

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.580
What is there to gain from searching for a junior officer?

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:11.170
Wha—?

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:14.840
Besides, our top priority is finding Lord Dolzief.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.880
We don't even know where he went down.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.420
Wasn't he shot down?

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:22.810
Tarjim!

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.930
After repairing the engines and replenishing our supplies,

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.390
you'll join the search team immediately.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.180
That's an order.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:31.760
Understood.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:39.050
<i>Still trying to win the favor of the dead, eh?</i>

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:44.530
No.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:48.740
No. I can't approve a search for Aoba-kun.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.160
Wh-Why? There's a storm outside, you know.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.790
We have to hurry and find Aoba-san...

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.960
That's exactly why.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.210
Thanks to the bad weather,

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.090
we managed to escape from the battle.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.550
But the enemy might still be nearby.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.080
The Valiancers and the Cygnus are damaged.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:11.310
Given our current situation,
ensuring the crew's safety is my top priority.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.440
Am I wrong, Lee-kun?

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.230
No, sir.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.690
But sir, Coupling requires both mechas to...

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.940
I considered everything before
making this decision, you know.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:27.030
The ship will remain on high alert.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.740
After the storm passes, we'll prepare for our departure.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:34.580
Just to be safe, the Valiancer team must be ready to fight at a moment's notice.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:39.420
Yes, sir.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.510
He sure acts like a kid.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:50.260
Huh?

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:53.640
Even after being told not to do it, he'll still do it.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:55.450
Definitely.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.480
Thank goodness. You finally woke up.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.070
Hey, wait. I didn't do anything!

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:12.790
You were sinking so I forced your
cockpit open and carried you here...

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.710
Oww...

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:20.920
I'll take you hostage and prove my innocence!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.050
I guess we're stuck here like this, eh?

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.300
My pack floated away, too.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.770
I'm going to check your Valiancer as well!

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:35.810
Okay...

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.870
This is a Coupling mecha.

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:46.280
This doesn't work either.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:50.220
I told you, didn't I? It stopped working.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:51.160
Oh well.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.700
I have his survival pack,

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:57.080
if worst comes to worst, we can always use the radio...

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.380
When it clears up a bit, I'll inspect it again.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.880
Aren't you being a little ungrateful?

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:12.600
We've finally met, but what the heck is this?

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.470
The hostage isn't allowed to talk nonsense.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:17.520
Put that down! That's my gun to begin with anyway.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.350
You let your pack get taken.
You're a terrible soldier, aren't you?

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.450
I'm not a soldier!

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.860
Wait, I am now.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:27.990
Why is someone like you piloting the new-type mecha?

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.030
Because you brought me here.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:30.820
What?

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:34.830
I was suddenly attacked by a Valiancer at school.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.040
Weren't you the one who saved me?

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:41.670
Then after saying "Dio is waiting for you",

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.540
you sent me here.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.460
To a world 70 years in the future.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:54.260
The Alliance must be really shorthanded to have someone like you piloting the new-type mecha.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.060
You really don't remember?

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:58.980
What are you talking about?

00:06:58.980 --> 00:06:59.810
Hina.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.020
Stop calling me by my first name and acting so personal.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:05.070
Why do you even know my name in the first place?

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:09.150
As I said before, you were my classmate, Yumihara Hina.

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:11.970
You saved me when I was attacked by a Valiancer—

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:13.070
That's enough!

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:15.370
Classmate? I Saved you?

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.660
Nothing you've said makes any sense!

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:19.410
Hina?

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.420
All I can say is this:

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:26.340
Even if I look like your Hina, I'm not her.

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:32.260
My father is in the Zogilian army,
the 101st Independent Patrol Force,

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.090
Lieutenant Commander Viktor Ryazan.

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:38.060
When I was 10, I was accepted into the
11th Military Preparatory Academy.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:42.690
After graduation, I was assigned to the 501st Mobile Unit.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:45.110
It's impossible for me to have made contact with you in school.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:47.440
Don't joke around! What the hell is that?

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.430
After going through all this to meet you—

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.870
Any further conversation is unnecessary.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:58.620
I'll let the Intelligence Department handle your interrogation.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:00.620
Hina...

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:12.660
Where are you going?

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:14.470
We've passed through the storm.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:15.720
I can fly now.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.600
That doesn't answer my question.

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:20.140
We can't afford to lose Luxon.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.390
I knew you'd say that.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.320
I have a message from the captain.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:33.400
You have three hours. If you can't find him
within that time frame, return immediately.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:37.870
Why are you following me?

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:40.990
It'd be troublesome if you went missing too.

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:44.290
There's a saying that the mummy hunter himself becomes a mummy.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.420
Do what you want.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:48.630
And one more thing, from Elvira-san.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:52.550
The Coupling machine might be able to help you.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:00.720
You still can't find Lord Dolzief?

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:03.310
We've been searching, but nothing so far.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:05.270
There's no way we'll find it.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:08.230
Looking for a mecha that's been shot down in this vast ocean.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.320
That's not true. Right, Bizon?

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:15.110
Oh, no. It's not about Fortuna.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:17.030
Since it just went down.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:18.820
Yeah, you're right.

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:22.700
Watch your mouth, Tarjim.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:27.500
Unlike us, Bizon has known Hina since they were kids.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.380
I got it. What a pain.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:52.900
I was in the same class as Hina,
but we hardly talked to each other.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:57.650
The first time we talked for any length was when she saved me.

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:02.600
The truth is, I don't know what kind of a girl she is nor what she likes.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.420
If I had the chance, there were
many things I wanted to ask her, like

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:10.040
"Why did you save me?"

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:13.710
or "How can I get back to my own time?"

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:18.470
And yet, just when I thought I'd finally met her,
you're telling me you're a completely different person.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:23.850
If that's the case, where did she go?

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:27.560
Maybe I can't return to my own time anymore.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:38.950
Hina?

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:39.490
Shh!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.450
Wh-What the hell?!

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:47.350
What is...?

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:01.260
What was that just now?

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.720
What happened?

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:05.510
I can't see a thing if you put out the fire! Hurry and—

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:06.720
You're too noisy! Shut up!

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:09.930
It wasn't me. It was blown out by the wind.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:11.770
There's gotta be one in the pack...

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:16.240
We're completely trapped.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.450
Are you kidding me?

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:23.370
Maybe we're lucky that the fire went out.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:27.410
Without fresh air, we'll eventually run out of oxygen.

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:28.910
Is that so?

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:34.330
H-Hey!

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.090
What are you doing?

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.630
Can't you tell?

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.470
I'm trying to dig my way out.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:43.720
Sorry, but I'm not going to lay
down and die here with an enemy.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.650
Then let me help too.

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:49.730
Two people will get the job done faster than one.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:51.980
Here, hurry up and untie me.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.150
I won't do anything in our current situation.

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.730
Besides, I don't want to die here either.

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:00.900
Very well.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.120
About time.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:12.120
If you try to do anything funny...

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:15.250
Don't worry, I won't.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.270
Damn it.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:51.540
How long will it take before we reach the outside?

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:55.000
After all this digging, the soil keeps falling down from the top.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.010
Alright. Break time is over.

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:07.840
Don't underestimate a former basketball player's stamina.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:24.320
The debris is coming from the top.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:29.450
It's probably easier to dig through there.

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:32.450
Yeah, you're right.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:12.200
As expected, that's the Commander of the Imperial Guard's mecha.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:14.370
Well, it's not like we didn't see this coming.

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:18.210
Bizon?

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:18.790
Hey.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:22.460
Hey, you. What are you doing?

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:24.380
The search is complete.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:25.670
What are you saying?

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:29.590
From now on, please allow my team to act on their own.

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:30.430
What are you...

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:33.390
The Commander's death has been confirmed.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.310
They've already completed their mission, right?

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.060
If that's the case,

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:39.390
Understood.

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:44.020
Hina.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.530
How have we still not found him?

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:52.490
It's been almost three hours.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:55.700
Maybe he was washed away by the ocean currents.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:59.460
If that's the case, we should extend the search area.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:02.960
If you're alive, hurry up and send out an SOS.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:18.680
<i>Damn. This is bad.</i>

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.480
<i>It's getting harder to breathe.</i>

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:22.100
<i>At this rate...</i>

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:27.230
Hina?

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.280
Hina! Hey, pull yourself together!

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:31.740
Hina!

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:33.990
<i>Could it be the lack of oxygen?</i>

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:49.040
I won't let you die.

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:50.760
I definitely won't let you die!

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:02.230
I... I...

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.270
What the...

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:23.000
<i>It's no use.</i>

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:35.180
<i>Am I going to die?</i>

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:38.930
<i>In this place? Now?</i>

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:54.030
Are you okay, Hina?

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:57.950
I'll pull you out.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:08.960
Are you okay?

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.090
You're not hurt?

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:14.510
Thank God.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:18.220
The pack drifted away.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:20.280
This time, we're really left with nothing.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.950
And now the cave is flooded, too.

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:27.270
We'll have to wait here until the storm stops.

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:28.270
If...

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:32.360
If we end up dying here...

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:41.350
Could it be?

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:47.330
Hey... Aob....

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:49.500
Can you hear... Please res...

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:50.420
Aoba.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:51.420
Dio.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:53.630
Alright. You okay?

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:56.130
Yeah. Thank God.

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:57.970
We have a message from Dio.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:00.720
He's found Aoba-san! He's alright!

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:06.560
Thank goodness.

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:12.730
It really is amazing, the Coupling System.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:21.740
By shifting to a wider Coupling field, they could
determine the Buddy's position and activate remotely.

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.620
What's the principle behind this?

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.120
It's "Love".

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:26.370
Beautiful.

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:28.160
What? Love?

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:30.830
Oh, come on. That's obviously a joke.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:35.300
However, this operating mode consumes a large amount of energy...

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:39.260
He had three hours and he's not back yet.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:41.930
I'll lecture him harshly later.

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:43.560
Go easy on him, okay?

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:47.060
He found him. So everything's fine now.

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:55.110
What's your situation?

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.860
What happened out there? Any sign of the enemy?

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:57.320
What?

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:58.950
E-Enemy?

00:18:58.950 --> 00:18:59.820
Um...

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:01.280
That's...

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:05.910
What's wrong? Hurry up and respond.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:07.550
Oh... it's...

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.580
Ah, the signal's breaking up!

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:11.080
What?

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:11.870
Aoba—

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:14.710
Hina.

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:17.210
What are Zogilia's communication channels?

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:17.840
What?

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:22.010
I'll call them so you can tell them you're here.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:34.730
Hina!

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:35.900
Have you found her?

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:37.730
Yeah, I have a fix on her signal.

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:38.740
Let's hurry.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:57.210
It's beautiful. Even after 70 years,
the sunrise never changes.

00:19:58.450 --> 00:19:59.630
Why?

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:03.720
Why did you let me call Zogilia?

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:08.220
Because if I didn't, you would've ended up being our prisoner.

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:11.100
I didn't want that to happen.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:14.310
You really are a terrible soldier, aren't you?

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:15.270
Yup.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.490
Dio's here.

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:25.070
Is your side coming to get you?

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:25.780
Yes...

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:28.870
Is that so? Well then, you'd better hide.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:30.750
You're right.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:33.290
Hold on!

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:37.130
This.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.210
Huh? What's this?

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:41.050
Hina's hairpin.

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:45.090
I brought it with me when I came here.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:46.010
I'm returning it.

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:48.390
But, I'm not that Hina.

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:51.770
I know. I just wanted you to have it.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.400
Here.

00:20:58.100 --> 00:20:59.860
Sorry. You can go now.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:02.740
U-Um...!

00:21:03.190 --> 00:21:05.200
I'm Watase Aoba.

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.450
I-I'm...

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:08.620
I know. See ya!

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:21.300
Yo, yo. Thank you for picking me up.

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:24.800
You bastard. Why'd you cut me off—?

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:29.010
I couldn't help it. It's not my fault that I lost the signal.

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:30.310
That's bull.

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:34.930
Well, isn't that fine? At least Aoba-kun
can return safely now.

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:36.310
That's right!

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:38.150
You'll be in trouble later.

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:41.400
What's that? Look who's talking, Dio.

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:43.190
What? What are you guys talking about?

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:44.400
Actually...

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.700
Fromm, recover Luxon and let's get out of here.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:50.410
Hey, wait! I'm not on board yet!

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:05.670
Watase Aoba.

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:19.020
With my heart, I call out

00:22:19.020 --> 00:22:23.390
To the far side, mutually drawn

00:22:23.390 --> 00:22:27.900
Forgetting even the reason I ache

00:22:27.900 --> 00:22:32.530
Just for now, please

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:36.700
I know you

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:41.200
I'm searching for you

00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:43.670
Softly pressing my lips

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:50.300
to the bright afterimage I can't keep from leaving

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:58.850
If hesitation is what gives way to the slightest of hopes

00:22:58.850 --> 00:23:03.430
To the many gentle mornings...

00:23:03.430 --> 00:23:07.980
and the times I have wondered

00:23:07.980 --> 00:23:12.240
In the future that leads back to that sky,

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:14.490
I want to save you,

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:16.570
I want to protect you

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:20.950
In the future that arrives at that dream

00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:23.830
Wait for me

00:23:23.830 --> 00:23:28.580
The love we'll surely find

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:33.380
I want you to reach out for it

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:38.420
Next episode, on Buddy Complex:

00:23:38.420 --> 00:23:40.010
"The Coupling System."
